          "description": "A chronic arterial disease characterized by the deposition of lipids, inflammatory cells, and other substances beneath the intima, forming plaques that lead to thickening, stiffening, and narrowing of arterial walls. It can affect arteries throughout the body and is the leading cause of coronary heart disease, stroke, and peripheral arterial disease."
        }
